<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15030" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρί-δηλος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰρῐ</span>], 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρί-δηλος</span></b>  (v. infr.), also
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρί-δᾱλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, in pr. n., <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			12(1).741
		</span></i> (<span class="entity">Rhodes</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>clear. distinct,far seen,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄσσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					130
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				94
			</span></i>; <i>bright,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀνταύγης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					237
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρίδηλον μνᾶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					7.52
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Megara</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Charito
				4.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>manifest,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάδε γὰρ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.65
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.276
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Chr.</u>
				35
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.331
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				690
			</span></i>; also 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΐδηλα</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Tyrt.
				11.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>conspicuous, magnificent,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγῶνα τῶν πρόσθεν -ότερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>An.</u>
					7.14.10
				</span></i>
			; <i>famous,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eun.
				<u>VS</u>
				p.456
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>(
				Comp.
			). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					2.26c
				</span></i>
			, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				948
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.451
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτατα</span> (sic) <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>—
				Ep.
			, 
				Ion.
			, and later Prose.</div>
